+production source maps. The build/development toolchain still needs review.
+
 Required follow-up, in order:
 
-1. Update or replace browser Axios 0.21.2 and review unused/build-only packages.
-   Preserve freshness, cancellation and timeout behavior. Review the
-   [deprecated CRA build](https://react.dev/blog/2025/02/14/sunsetting-create-react-app)
-   separately from the completed backend changes.
+1. Resolve the 73 remaining build-tool findings and supported build/test matrix,
+   including the [deprecated CRA build](https://react.dev/blog/2025/02/14/sunsetting-create-react-app).
+   Preserve the tested browser behavior. Review the used UI libraries'
+   maintenance separately; absence of an advisory is not a support guarantee.
+   Include the legacy map dependency tree's Acorn path; a CRA replacement
+   alone does not clear every installed dependency path.
 2. Select and verify the final Node/npm matrix and combined clean installation.
-   Replace the inherited Node 16/`npm install`/foundation S3 workflow before
-   enabling deployment. No workflow has been run for these changes.
+   The replacement validation workflow pins local test versions and has not
+   run on GitHub. Public deployment remains separate work.
 3. Select and record the GeoIP dataset and its terms/attribution. Accept the
    protected update workflow, failure/recovery and refresh/deletion schedule
    before public use; package compatibility does not establish fresh data.
@@ -60,5 +69,5 @@ Required follow-up, in order:
 
 The accompanying efsn investigation retains the original review in
 `docs/restart-dashboard-runtime.md` and the latest follow-up in
-`docs/restart-dashboard-geoip.md`, with exact package and local test evidence
+`docs/restart-dashboard-frontend.md`, with exact package and local test evidence
 under their corresponding `docs/evidence/` directories.
